                        ],
                        "form": "астроно́ме"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "12505393-3025-43fc-bf1b-3e72257d9c60",
                        "entry_id": "9cebc4b4-8d4d-33a2-a0bd-8bfe2a959218",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "астроно́мах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                        "entry_id": "9cebc4b4-8d4d-33a2-a0bd-8bfe2a959218",
                        "glosses": [
                            "учёный, занимающийся астрономией, то есть исследующий расположение, строение, свойства, происхождение и развитие небесных тел и их систем"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bf6794b-cb4a-4ba5-8dd3-bee85377d05d",
                                "sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                                "text": "Случились вместе два астро́нома в пиру // И спорили весьма между собой в жару."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0885a6d-d817-45bb-a4b8-a7ccd882dbba",
                                "sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                                "text": "Астро́номы и богословы, // Свой мозг пыля из года в год, // Схоластики средневековой // Здесь собирали горький мёд."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f31d11c-44dc-4d9f-9753-6ee582c98b3b",
                                "sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                                "text": "Таким образом, первым, кто увидел (но не понял) реликтовое излучение, был ещё в 1939 г. канадский астроном Мак-Келлер."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "903adb02-5177-449d-834f-7a61e2b8b23b",
                                "sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                                "text": "В 1916 году русский астроном Сергей Белявский открыл малую планету под номером 852."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82a2e6b0-470a-42fc-a54b-b9e571a81931",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cebc4b4-8d4d-33a2-a0bd-8bfe2a959218",
                        "source_sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                        "target_lang_word": "astronomer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "astronomer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9cf45b3-b0f1-35f2-8517-d0d0dd8049a6",
                                        "entry_id": "e748b9f3-c0f4-389b-864c-8c083bcc7919",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who studies astronomy, the stars or the physical universe; a scientist whose area of research is astronomy or astrophysics."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "901b57a3-d6a5-441a-9a06-c11743021904",
                                                "sense_id": "b9cf45b3-b0f1-35f2-8517-d0d0dd8049a6",
                                                "text": "Pioneering American astronomer Vera Rubin once mentored fellow aspiring female astronomers and advocated for women in science. It’s fitting that the first national US observatory named for a female astronomer is in her honor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f04166-e891-4d7a-a35f-902e5b52c6c8",
                                                "sense_id": "b9cf45b3-b0f1-35f2-8517-d0d0dd8049a6",
                                                "text": "But none of those brown dwarfs were speeding along on a trajectory that would carry them out of the galaxy like “runaway” hypervelocity stars observed by astronomers in the last two decades."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "33d23dd5-6438-4286-9770-7c49bc439b0c",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cebc4b4-8d4d-33a2-a0bd-8bfe2a959218",
                        "source_sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
                        "target_lang_word": "stargazer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "stargazer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9cb26633-c9f4-3ab3-892b-5bc7e5988aad",
                                        "entry_id": "5540c828-740d-3549-9608-a23615c01a41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who gazes at the stars; an astronomer or astrologer (now especially an amateur one)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "244d0ebe-ceed-4885-8f0f-b75b54510fa7",
                                                "sense_id": "9cb26633-c9f4-3ab3-892b-5bc7e5988aad",
                                                "text": "Thou art wearied in the multitude of thy counsels: let now the astrologers, the starre-gazers, the monethly prognosticators stand vp, and saue thee from these things that shall come vpon thee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff66f21c-0362-4d2d-adaf-8a26fb77b405",
                                                "sense_id": "9cb26633-c9f4-3ab3-892b-5bc7e5988aad",
                                                "text": "[…] the four satellites of Jupiter, which, it is thought, were probably visible to certain of the more sharp-sighted stargazers of ancient Babylonia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dd75f12-d1ee-307d-be24-b43c4bda5d3b",
                                        "entry_id": "5540c828-740d-3549-9608-a23615c01a41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of family Uranoscopidae of bottom-dwelling fish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "423838ca-df71-46d5-878c-cab45d92a3d9",
                                                "sense_id": "1dd75f12-d1ee-307d-be24-b43c4bda5d3b",
                                                "text": "A stargazer is a frightening fish by any sretch of the imagination, but not until the day I first saw one in its own world did I understand its true nature."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62961682-7afe-481e-a9cb-a19994117114",
                        "source_entry_id": "9cebc4b4-8d4d-33a2-a0bd-8bfe2a959218",
                        "source_sense_id": "455dc8b1-fe81-3078-af69-331c5febcb6c",
